  "scopeLimit": "Using a real new Stage1 project, current input version, application-owned reservation, saved instruction and actual exported ZIP package, the invalid response must be rejected with its literal expected diagnostic and no proposal. Preparation and actual operational save/reload preserve the whole canonical project snapshot: every Job field except CURRENT_STATE/NEXT_REQUIRED_ACTION, all registered and nonregistry canonical values, all stage values except gate/status/derivedData/responseDraft, the selected reservation binding/contentSha256 and all other reservations, canonical revision, identities, versions, pointers and root metadata. Exact operational raw/audit collections and recomputed projectSha256 are excluded from that snapshot comparison, while all preexisting audit prefixes remain byte/value-equivalent. The original input object remains unchanged. These are synthetic controlled actor inputs under the production storage owner with an isolated transaction adapter; no browser, external actor, authenticated human decision, stage completion or acceptance is claimed. The maintained assertions require three directly exercised conforming response-file controls to remain valid pending proposals, retain exact raw bytes, and commit no canonical changes. Curly quotation characters used as authoritative JSON delimiters must produce the sole UNSAFE_SMART_QUOTES error; correctly ASCII-delimited JSON containing escaped or Unicode quotation data remains valid.",
